# No lazy shortcuts

Fix the failure. Do not hide it.

- NEVER empty `catch`, blind `catch`, or `catch` / `catchAll` that returns
  `null` or `false` to suppress an error. Use `Data.TaggedError`, `Match`, or
  `Option`.
- NEVER `new Promise` to wrap an API that already returns a promise or Effect.
- NEVER fire-and-forget (`void promise`, ignored calls). Await the promise or
  return the Effect.
- NEVER `sleep` / `setTimeout` to paper over a race. Wait on the real signal.
- NEVER tautological tests (`expect(true)`, asserting a value the test just
  assigned).
